7. System Hacking kya hai?

System hacking ka broad meaning hai computer system ki security ko test karna aur unauthorized access/privilege-related weaknesses identify karna.

Ethical hacking mein ye authorized environment mein kiya jata hai.

System hacking ke major stages:

Gaining Access
Privilege Escalation
Maintaining Access
Covering Tracks
8. Gaining Access

Is stage ka objective system mein access obtain karna hota hai.

Possible weaknesses:

Weak passwords
Vulnerable services
Unpatched software
Misconfiguration
Application vulnerabilities
9. Password Attacks ⭐

Passwords authentication ka important part hain.

Common password attack concepts:

Brute Force

Possible combinations systematically try karna.

Dictionary Attack

Common words/password lists use karke password guess karna.

Hybrid Attack

Dictionary words ke saath numbers/symbols/variations combine karke guessing.

Credential Stuffing

Previously leaked username-password combinations ko doosri services par try karna.

10. Privilege Escalation ⭐⭐⭐

Agar attacker low-privileged account se system mein enter karta hai, to higher privileges obtain karne ki attempt ko Privilege Escalation kehte hain.

Vertical Privilege Escalation

Low privilege → high privilege.

Example:

Normal User → Administrator/Root

Horizontal Privilege Escalation

Same privilege level ke kisi doosre user's resources access karna.

Example:

User A kisi weakness ki wajah se User B ka data access kar le.

Yaad rakho:

Vertical = Level up
Horizontal = Same level, different user

11. Maintaining Access

System mein access milne ke baad attacker access ko future mein maintain karne ki attempt kar sakta hai.

Ethical security testing mein is concept ko controlled environment mein evaluate kiya jata hai.

12. Covering Tracks

Attacker apni activity ke evidence ko hide/remove karne ki attempt kar sakta hai.

Security perspective se important evidence:

Logs
Authentication records
File changes
Network activity

Isliye logging and monitoring security ke liye important hain.

MODULE 7 — Malware
13. Malware kya hai? ⭐

Malware = Malicious Software

Aisa software jo system ko harm karne, unauthorized access lene, information steal karne ya unwanted activity perform karne ke liye design kiya gaya ho.

14. Virus

Virus ek malicious program/code hota hai jo generally kisi host file/program se attach hokar spread karta hai.

Usually execution ke liye host/user interaction required ho sakta hai.

Keyword:

Virus → Host-dependent

15. Worm ⭐

Worm self-replicating malware hota hai jo networks/systems ke through automatically spread kar sakta hai.

Virus vs Worm

Virus → host file/program ke saath attach

Worm → independently replicate/spread

16. Trojan ⭐

Trojan legitimate/useful software ke form mein appear kar sakta hai but internally malicious functionality contain karta hai.

Example:

User ko lagta hai ki woh useful application install kar raha hai, but application malicious activity perform karti hai.

Keyword:

Trojan → Disguise

17. Spyware

Spyware secretly user/system ki information monitor ya collect karne ke liye use hota hai.

Possible targets:

User activity
Browsing information
Sensitive information
18. Keylogger

Keylogger keystrokes record karne ke liye designed software/hardware ho sakta hai.

Potentially capture:

Usernames
Passwords
Messages
Other typed information
19. Ransomware ⭐⭐⭐

Ransomware victim ke files/system ko encrypt ya otherwise inaccessible bana sakta hai aur attacker payment demand kar sakta hai.

Simple flow:

Infection → Data inaccessible → Ransom demand

Protection:

Regular backups
Patching
Endpoint protection
Email security
User awareness
Network segmentation
20. Rootkit

Rootkit ka purpose system mein malicious presence ko hide karna aur privileged access maintain karna ho sakta hai.

Keyword:

Rootkit → Hide + Privileged access

21. Botnet

Botnet = Compromised devices ka network

Compromised devices ko attacker remotely control kar sakta hai.

Botnets ka use:

DDoS
Spam
Malware distribution
Other malicious activities

mein ho sakta hai.

22. Malware Distribution Methods

Malware system tak different ways se pahunch sakta hai:

Malicious email attachment
Malicious links
Compromised websites
Untrusted software
Removable media
Malvertising
Social engineering
